1
00:00:00,691 --> 00:00:01,802
(About Ms. Suda…)

2
00:00:02,170 --> 00:00:03,197
(Ms. Suda?)

3
00:00:04,555 --> 00:00:05,902
(Why did you do this?)

4
00:00:05,950 --> 00:00:09,247
The fact that she abandoned your class
and refused to continue teaching

5
00:00:10,016 --> 00:00:12,016
was a serious dereliction of her duty
as a teacher.

6
00:00:12,340 --> 00:00:13,798
As student council president,

7
00:00:14,237 --> 00:00:15,900
I can’t let this continue.

8
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:19,490
Do you wanna wipe your face?

9
00:02:06,850 --> 00:02:07,850
You’ve got everything?

10
00:02:07,998 --> 00:02:09,202
I think so, mom.

11
00:02:09,570 --> 00:02:11,804
But I saw a toothbrush on the table.

12
00:02:12,810 --> 00:02:14,002
That I forgot.

13
00:02:15,050 --> 00:02:16,700
Hurry, you’re gonna miss the bus.

14
00:02:17,234 --> 00:02:20,167
We’re so early.
I don’t think the bus has arrived yet.

15
00:02:20,207 --> 00:02:21,503
We have to make sure.

16
00:02:22,402 --> 00:02:24,484
I’m just going on a school trip.

17
00:02:24,506 --> 00:02:26,797
Why are you guys so excited?

18
00:02:27,550 --> 00:02:29,120
Well, you’ve never done this before.

19
00:02:29,150 --> 00:02:30,779
Of course, I’m excited.

20
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,620
- Let’s go.
- See you, Mom.

21
00:02:34,660 --> 00:02:37,500
(This is my very first school trip.)

22
00:02:37,757 --> 00:02:40,623
(This will be a trip I’ll never forget.)

23
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:41,840
Let’s go, Dad.

24
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:54,296
1…2…3.

25
00:02:55,518 --> 00:02:56,820
Okay.

26
00:02:57,370 --> 00:02:59,656
If anyone wants to make a donation,
there’s a booth over to the side.

27
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:02,285
And those who want to pray
can head upstairs.

28
00:03:02,325 --> 00:03:04,053
See you on the bus in half an hour.

29
00:03:04,274 --> 00:03:05,274
Let’s go.

30
00:03:05,712 --> 00:03:06,987
Come on, Ji. Let’s see the elephant.

31
00:03:07,011 --> 00:03:08,011
Elephant?

32
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:26,330
I give up.

33
00:03:27,143 --> 00:03:28,411
Let’s donate some coins instead.

34
00:03:28,435 --> 00:03:29,743
It’s so freaking hot here.

35
00:03:29,770 --> 00:03:32,180
No way, Kong. I won’t give up that easy.

36
00:03:32,797 --> 00:03:34,600
I should have stayed in my damned room.

37
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:37,200
Language! We’re at a temple.

38
00:03:37,571 --> 00:03:38,571
Ugh.

39
00:03:40,910 --> 00:03:41,976
We’ll be here all day.

40
00:03:43,001 --> 00:03:45,370
The bus is leaving at 10.

41
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:46,697
Why are you guys still here?

42
00:03:46,970 --> 00:03:50,004
Ty said he wouldn’t leave
until he successfully threw the coin.

43
00:03:50,420 --> 00:03:51,622
Class 7.

44
00:03:52,860 --> 00:03:54,247
Why aren’t you on the bus yet?

45
00:03:54,922 --> 00:03:57,530
And Kongpob,
you’re the last person from class 9.

46
00:03:57,750 --> 00:04:00,463
Ty won’t leave until he can throw the coin
in the elephant’s mouth.

47
00:04:01,546 --> 00:04:04,137
Okay, Tyler.
I’ll give you one more chance.

48
00:04:04,390 --> 00:04:07,297
Okay, I’ll get it this time.

49
00:04:24,134 --> 00:04:25,404
See? I did it.

50
00:04:25,734 --> 00:04:26,623
How did I do?

51
00:04:26,642 --> 00:04:28,198
- Spectacular.
- Did I do well, guys?

52
00:04:28,430 --> 00:04:29,200
Amazing.
Go.

53
00:04:29,951 --> 00:04:32,182
Get on the bus. Kongpob, you too.

54
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:32,693
Yes.

55
00:04:32,711 --> 00:04:33,711
Come on.

56
00:04:35,305 --> 00:04:36,503
Kong, wait for me!

57
00:04:37,382 --> 00:04:38,382
Come on, Kong.

58
00:05:01,309 --> 00:05:02,949
Why aren’t you guys having fun like them?

59
00:05:20,973 --> 00:05:23,245
Want some popsicles?

60
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:24,902
Do you want some popsicles?

61
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:28,004
Here, my brother.

62
00:05:29,910 --> 00:05:30,602
Thank you.

63
00:05:30,777 --> 00:05:32,297
I guarantee it’s so good.

64
00:05:33,592 --> 00:05:34,992
Don’t you wanna take a look around?

65
00:05:41,454 --> 00:05:42,494
Wanna go together?

66
00:05:48,048 --> 00:05:50,702
Popsicle? Tyler made this himself.

67
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:53,302
Can we get another one?

68
00:06:07,090 --> 00:06:08,100
Here, Ji.

69
00:06:14,582 --> 00:06:16,502
That was… a bit weird.

70
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:23,970
TRADITIONAL THAI COFFEE

71
00:06:33,933 --> 00:06:34,933
You want some?

72
00:06:36,426 --> 00:06:40,380
You can sense my thirst
coming through my skin?

73
00:06:41,780 --> 00:06:42,780
Mmm.

74
00:06:44,065 --> 00:06:45,065
Let’s go.

75
00:06:50,173 --> 00:06:52,299
- Can I have an iced cocoa?
- Of course.

76
00:06:54,939 --> 00:06:55,939
I’ll have the same.

77
00:06:57,020 --> 00:06:58,097
Make that two, please.

78
00:06:58,576 --> 00:06:59,576
Sure.

79
00:07:01,100 --> 00:07:03,459
- Here.
- Oh, no. I got this.

80
00:07:04,490 --> 00:07:05,490
It’s okay.

81
00:07:17,675 --> 00:07:18,675
I’ll take…

82
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:29,102
For the cocoa.

83
00:07:40,130 --> 00:07:41,250
What’s this, Ji?

84
00:07:42,127 --> 00:07:43,598
Looks like a gymnast.

85
00:07:45,860 --> 00:07:48,300
That’s a sugar sculpture
of a fishing monkey.

86
00:07:48,524 --> 00:07:50,000
- Sugar sculpture?
- Mmm.

87
00:07:50,291 --> 00:07:51,737
So it’s edible?

88
00:07:51,777 --> 00:07:52,777
Umm…

89
00:07:53,075 --> 00:07:54,228
This is for Ruth.

90
00:07:54,270 --> 00:07:56,666
- If you want it…
- You can have it. I’m good.

91
00:07:57,081 --> 00:07:58,462
Really? I’ll take this one then.

92
00:08:01,053 --> 00:08:02,053
Come on, Kong.

93
00:08:03,380 --> 00:08:04,380
What?

94
00:08:04,451 --> 00:08:05,496
Thank you, Ji.

95
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:13,260
This one’s not bitten.
You can take a bite.

96
00:08:17,312 --> 00:08:18,312
Hey.

97
00:08:50,521 --> 00:08:52,398
Hey, I said just a bite.

98
00:08:55,854 --> 00:08:57,201
I said just a bite.

99
00:08:57,466 --> 00:08:58,625
You ate the whole thing.

100
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:00,574
Eat it.

101
00:09:26,878 --> 00:09:27,900
Doesn’t look like me.

102
00:09:28,109 --> 00:09:29,109
It does.

103
00:09:45,342 --> 00:09:46,342
That one.

104
00:09:46,441 --> 00:09:47,614
- Which one?
- The red one.

105
00:09:50,767 --> 00:09:52,822
Yes, see how good I am?

106
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:54,050
Thank you.

107
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:55,920
Here.

108
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,500
- Huh?
- Take it.

109
00:09:58,010 --> 00:09:59,666
I’ve won so many of these.

110
00:10:01,090 --> 00:10:02,345
So cute. A big one.

111
00:10:07,592 --> 00:10:08,847
-Mr. Tin
-Huh?

112
00:10:08,877 --> 00:10:10,472
Take a picture for us.

113
00:10:10,502 --> 00:10:11,340
Oh, wow.

114
00:10:11,505 --> 00:10:13,428
Open your eyes. Don’t fear the sun.

115
00:10:13,450 --> 00:10:14,602
It’s too bright.

116
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:16,219
1…2…

117
00:10:22,850 --> 00:10:23,998
Hey, look at that.

118
00:10:27,442 --> 00:10:28,442
What?

119
00:10:34,014 --> 00:10:35,638
- More, more.
- More?

120
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:58,462
NAVINA SCHOOL

121
00:10:58,493 --> 00:11:00,470
We’re here, everybody!

122
00:11:00,866 --> 00:11:02,459
Don’t forget your bags.

123
00:11:02,720 --> 00:11:04,435
Watch your steps, guys.

124
00:11:04,645 --> 00:11:06,300
We have to go down first.

125
00:11:07,134 --> 00:11:08,134
Come on.

126
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:11,085
Let’s go, Ji. Go, go, go.

127
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:12,750
Come on, come on, come on.

128
00:11:14,168 --> 00:11:15,697
Come along, everyone.

129
00:11:16,314 --> 00:11:17,499
Okay, you’re all here?

130
00:11:17,881 --> 00:11:21,220
Class 7, you can take your stuff
up to your rooms.

131
00:11:21,512 --> 00:11:23,401
Enjoy yourselves, everyone.

132
00:11:23,432 --> 00:11:24,742
See you at dinner.

133
00:11:24,790 --> 00:11:26,610
- Go.
- Let’s go.

134
00:11:26,634 --> 00:11:28,740
Go, Ji. Let’s go.

135
00:11:34,628 --> 00:11:36,700
You guys go on
a fancy trip like this every year?

136
00:11:36,885 --> 00:11:39,400
No, it’s usually a one-day trip.

137
00:11:39,798 --> 00:11:41,703
Or we go camping in the wild.

138
00:11:42,237 --> 00:11:45,097
This is the first year
we get to stay at a seaside hotel.

139
00:11:45,374 --> 00:11:49,210
Actually, this hotel is
part of the president’s family business,

140
00:11:49,490 --> 00:11:52,897
so we’re getting
some luxurious perks this year.

141
00:11:53,225 --> 00:11:54,494
- For real?
- Umm.

142
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:56,902
Why does his family send him
to a public school, then?

143
00:11:57,048 --> 00:11:59,254
Why not send him to study abroad?

144
00:11:59,789 --> 00:12:02,263
I heard he asked his dad
back in middle school,

145
00:12:02,296 --> 00:12:04,097
but his dad wouldn’t let him go.

146
00:12:05,697 --> 00:12:07,462
I’ll put my things away.
See you downstairs.

147
00:12:07,685 --> 00:12:08,685
See you.

148
00:12:10,872 --> 00:12:12,300
Our room is that way. Come on, Ji.

149
00:12:13,266 --> 00:12:15,230
Hurry, Ji. Change your clothes
and we’ll get in the water.

150
00:12:15,254 --> 00:12:16,622
I’m still feeling car sick.

151
00:12:16,650 --> 00:12:17,952
I’ll get some rest first.

152
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:20,303
Do you want me to stay with you?

153
00:12:21,830 --> 00:12:24,150
No, go ahead. I’m just feeling dizzy.

154
00:12:24,182 --> 00:12:25,620
Just need to lay down for a bit.

155
00:12:26,324 --> 00:12:27,383
See you later then.

156
00:13:12,957 --> 00:13:15,435
Come on. Go, go, go.

157
00:13:15,469 --> 00:13:16,469
Go back.

158
00:13:19,059 --> 00:13:20,700
What? What’s going on?

159
00:13:25,014 --> 00:13:26,400
Come on down and play with us.

160
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:26,170
Won’t you go play in the water with them?

161
00:14:27,771 --> 00:14:29,802
No, I can’t get in the water today.

162
00:14:35,749 --> 00:14:36,802
You’re drawing again?

163
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:42,001
You don’t get opportunities like this
very often.

164
00:14:44,112 --> 00:14:48,180
Ji, do you think I’ll get into law school?

165
00:14:53,680 --> 00:14:58,160
PHAPPIM, LAWYER, IS NOT WORRIED
THAT THE OPPOSING PARTY IS INFLUENTIAL.
“UNDUE INFLUENCE CANNOT OVERRIDE THE LAW.”

166
00:14:58,200 --> 00:15:01,602
(Not only will you get into law school,
but you’ll also be a great lawyer.)

167
00:15:03,862 --> 00:15:05,297
I know you will.

168
00:15:08,420 --> 00:15:12,198
My parents said
I could do whatever I want if I get in,

169
00:15:13,550 --> 00:15:17,404
but If I get in,
I’ll be busy with university exams.

170
00:15:17,868 --> 00:15:19,486
After graduation,
I’ll have to take the bar exam

171
00:15:19,510 --> 00:15:20,902
and the Thai Barrister exam, too.

172
00:15:23,419 --> 00:15:25,420
Do you think I’ll have time to draw?

173
00:15:28,939 --> 00:15:30,823
Why wait until then?

174
00:15:34,484 --> 00:15:36,500
You’re going to succeed anyway.

175
00:15:38,565 --> 00:15:40,300
- You’re that sure?
- Mmm.

176
00:15:46,445 --> 00:15:47,445
Thanks.

177
00:16:11,522 --> 00:16:13,702
Oh, you’re leaving?

178
00:16:14,183 --> 00:16:15,859
The sun hasn’t even set yet.

179
00:16:16,281 --> 00:16:18,703
Yeah, I’ve finished sketching.

180
00:16:19,248 --> 00:16:21,602
I’m going to color it in by the pool.

181
00:16:21,965 --> 00:16:23,499
I can enjoy the view from there.

182
00:16:24,005 --> 00:16:25,102
Besides…

183
00:16:27,630 --> 00:16:29,571
I’ll leave now. See you at dinner.

184
00:16:40,111 --> 00:16:41,150
Stay here with me.

185
00:16:48,974 --> 00:16:50,900
The president’s not joining us?

186
00:16:51,164 --> 00:16:54,300
Mr. Wira called him in
to discuss the science project.

187
00:16:55,200 --> 00:16:57,899
It's been since we checked in.
I wonder if they’re done yet.

188
00:16:58,430 --> 00:16:59,430
They are.

189
00:16:59,620 --> 00:17:01,970
I saw him watching the sunset
with Ji by the beach.

190
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:03,598
Oh, those two again.

191
00:17:04,465 --> 00:17:06,700
I saw them wandering around
at the market, too.

192
00:17:07,357 --> 00:17:10,137
And the president always stares at Ji
while he eats.

193
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:12,099
Do you think…

194
00:17:12,851 --> 00:17:14,601
I thought that too at first.

195
00:17:14,973 --> 00:17:19,937
But when I watched them closely,
it seemed like there was something more.

196
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:23,525
Lita, did the president and Ji
have some history together?

197
00:17:23,582 --> 00:17:26,660
Other than Ji hitting him in the face
with a volleyball, no.

198
00:17:26,768 --> 00:17:28,099
You’ve noticed it too?

199
00:17:28,401 --> 00:17:29,401
Mmm.

200
00:17:29,625 --> 00:17:31,100
If you keep staring at someone,

201
00:17:31,677 --> 00:17:35,617
unless you’re interested in them
or have a crush on them,

202
00:17:36,887 --> 00:17:38,502
there probably isn’t any other reason.

203
00:17:38,675 --> 00:17:42,896
I think he’s interested but…

204
00:17:43,408 --> 00:17:46,500
Ruth has been working
harder than usual lately,

205
00:17:47,290 --> 00:17:49,349
both with the Ms. Suda situation

206
00:17:49,737 --> 00:17:53,299
and getting Ji
involved in various activities.

207
00:17:53,565 --> 00:17:56,096
Hmm, maybe I’m overthinking it,

208
00:17:56,140 --> 00:17:58,699
but I feel like
he’s more attached to Ji than usual.

209
00:18:14,030 --> 00:18:16,190
Would you be interested in joining
the student council?

210
00:18:21,303 --> 00:18:24,779
One of our members
is leaving to study elsewhere,

211
00:18:25,724 --> 00:18:28,300
so we have an opening,
if you’re interested.

212
00:18:32,285 --> 00:18:34,404
No, I’ll have to pass.

213
00:18:37,268 --> 00:18:40,214
The student council
organizes lots of activities.

214
00:18:40,970 --> 00:18:42,500
You’ll get to meet new people.

215
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:46,260
Students from other grades
will get to know you better too.

216
00:18:47,310 --> 00:18:48,600
You should ask someone else.

217
00:18:51,640 --> 00:18:52,699
Are you sure?

218
00:18:53,554 --> 00:18:56,416
You can take your time to think about it.

219
00:18:56,722 --> 00:18:59,001
No, don’t waste your time on me.

220
00:19:00,078 --> 00:19:03,619
There are others
who are willing to do it anyway.

221
00:19:06,337 --> 00:19:09,777
Won’t you regret it
if you miss this opportunity?

222
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:13,601
No. Why would I regret it?

223
00:19:13,970 --> 00:19:15,850
It’s just not becoming
a student council member.

224
00:19:22,925 --> 00:19:24,601
You wouldn’t regret it even if you died?

225
00:19:37,130 --> 00:19:38,130
No.

226
00:19:40,210 --> 00:19:42,248
There’s absolutely nothing to regret.

227
00:19:46,530 --> 00:19:47,530
What about you?

228
00:19:50,197 --> 00:19:51,197
Me?

229
00:19:51,580 --> 00:19:53,202
I looked out over the balcony

230
00:19:53,230 --> 00:19:55,130
and didn’t see you hanging out
with the others.

231
00:19:55,162 --> 00:19:56,216
Where did you go?

232
00:19:57,134 --> 00:20:00,899
Oh, Mr. Wira called me in
to discuss the science project.

233
00:20:01,269 --> 00:20:04,000
Then we went to talk to the hotel manager.

234
00:20:04,380 --> 00:20:06,546
- After that, we…
- That’s enough.

235
00:20:07,971 --> 00:20:10,598
Did I say something wrong?

236
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:12,320
No, it’s just…

237
00:20:14,045 --> 00:20:15,259
Don’t you ever get tired.

238
00:20:21,081 --> 00:20:22,081
Not really.

239
00:20:23,269 --> 00:20:24,697
As the class president,

240
00:20:25,183 --> 00:20:26,598
that’s what I have to do.

241
00:20:26,979 --> 00:20:27,979
Have to do?

242
00:20:28,491 --> 00:20:30,171
That means you don’t really want to do it.

243
00:20:30,386 --> 00:20:31,500
I want to.

244
00:20:33,598 --> 00:20:34,598
But…

245
00:20:35,582 --> 00:20:36,582
I…

246
00:20:48,468 --> 00:20:51,401
Why don’t you take a break from it
for a while?

247
00:20:56,303 --> 00:20:58,336
I don’t mean quitting the student council,

248
00:20:59,334 --> 00:21:02,000
because I know you’re dedicated to it.

249
00:21:03,767 --> 00:21:05,539
But now you’re doing everything.

250
00:21:06,139 --> 00:21:08,305
- You’re taking on too much.
- But if I stop…

251
00:21:10,490 --> 00:21:11,545
What about everyone else?

252
00:21:14,632 --> 00:21:18,139
No one would be mad at you
if you were a little selfish.

253
00:21:19,195 --> 00:21:21,050
Even if someone did get mad, so what?

254
00:21:21,419 --> 00:21:22,601
Why should you care?

255
00:21:31,456 --> 00:21:34,001
You think I can just quit?

256
00:21:34,331 --> 00:21:35,604
Oh, why not?

257
00:21:35,736 --> 00:21:38,296
I thought you could step down
from some of your responsibilities.

258
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:43,177
I can, but…

259
00:21:59,130 --> 00:22:00,497
You haven’t changed at all.

260
00:22:12,608 --> 00:22:13,801
The sun has set.

261
00:22:14,868 --> 00:22:15,868
I’m sorry.

262
00:22:16,549 --> 00:22:18,303
I made you miss such a special moment.

263
00:22:20,170 --> 00:22:21,497
I wouldn’t call it missing out.

264
00:22:22,910 --> 00:22:24,097
It’s better, actually.

265
00:22:25,330 --> 00:22:26,330
What is?

266
00:22:27,001 --> 00:22:29,097
Getting to talk to you.

267
00:22:32,020 --> 00:22:33,543
Talking to you…

268
00:22:34,330 --> 00:22:37,001
makes me happier than watching the sunset.

269
00:22:47,630 --> 00:22:48,630
Ji.

270
00:22:48,816 --> 00:22:49,816
Hmm?

271
00:22:52,130 --> 00:22:53,130
Jiraphat.

272
00:22:59,470 --> 00:23:00,470
Thank you.

273
00:23:37,280 --> 00:23:39,602
Poked on the left butt,
poked on the right butt

274
00:23:41,634 --> 00:23:43,977
Poked on the left butt,
poked on the right butt

275
00:23:44,111 --> 00:23:46,139
Really hot, really hot, really hot!

276
00:24:00,208 --> 00:24:02,820
That was Class 1’s Cinderella performance!

277
00:24:02,856 --> 00:24:05,297
Let’s give them a round of applause!

278
00:24:19,840 --> 00:24:22,013
Class 7, gather around. Come here.

279
00:24:22,040 --> 00:24:24,318
Come on, come on.

280
00:24:24,358 --> 00:24:27,296
- When can we go back to our rooms?
- Oh, stop complaining.

281
00:24:27,370 --> 00:24:31,139
When you guys see what I brought,
you won’t want to get back to your rooms.

282
00:24:31,300 --> 00:24:32,899
Tada!

283
00:24:35,961 --> 00:24:37,810
Pass these around and go have fun.

284
00:24:37,842 --> 00:24:40,700
- Give these to your friends.
- Okay, I’ll pass them around.

285
00:24:40,820 --> 00:24:42,146
Yeah, and be careful.

286
00:24:42,220 --> 00:24:45,500
- Remember not to leave them on the ground.
- Come on, Ji. Come on, come on.

287
00:24:47,430 --> 00:24:48,430
Here.

288
00:24:49,382 --> 00:24:51,296
Oh, where’s the light?

289
00:24:52,130 --> 00:24:53,130
Hey, Kong.

290
00:24:56,194 --> 00:24:58,057
Did you sneak out to smoke again?

291
00:24:58,540 --> 00:25:00,690
Ty, that smoking thing is history.

292
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:02,200
This is not my light.

293
00:25:02,346 --> 00:25:04,663
They all lit their sparklers so I took it.

294
00:25:07,140 --> 00:25:08,937
What? I thought you needed it.

295
00:25:08,962 --> 00:25:10,340
- Do you want it or not?
- Of course.

296
00:25:10,377 --> 00:25:11,700
Light this for me, Ji.

297
00:25:12,075 --> 00:25:14,201
Do you even know how to use it?

298
00:25:14,630 --> 00:25:16,860
Of course.
I used to play with these with my dad.

299
00:25:16,887 --> 00:25:18,620
Don’t worry. I got this.

300
00:25:19,460 --> 00:25:20,331
Just light it.

301
00:25:20,364 --> 00:25:21,964
If something goes wrong, I’ll handle it.

302
00:25:25,545 --> 00:25:26,614
Here I come.

303
00:25:26,894 --> 00:25:27,700
Ji!

304
00:25:27,770 --> 00:25:29,299
Woohoo woohoo!

305
00:25:31,877 --> 00:25:34,401
Kongpob, Tyler, stop fooling around.

306
00:25:34,539 --> 00:25:39,002
Cut them some slack. Let them have fun.

307
00:25:39,708 --> 00:25:41,259
I’m watching them.

308
00:25:41,670 --> 00:25:44,259
If things get out of hand,
I’ll shut it down.

309
00:25:44,768 --> 00:25:45,768
Ji!

310
00:25:48,645 --> 00:25:49,645
Take this.

311
00:25:49,865 --> 00:25:50,865
You missed.

312
00:26:02,140 --> 00:26:03,140
Hey.

313
00:26:03,920 --> 00:26:05,096
Don’t you want to light it?

314
00:26:09,986 --> 00:26:11,420
If you’re scared of fire,

315
00:26:11,457 --> 00:26:13,857
I’ll light it for you
and then you take it.

316
00:26:16,870 --> 00:26:18,000
(Scared of fire?)

317
00:26:18,669 --> 00:26:20,656
(Why did I say that?)

318
00:26:20,790 --> 00:26:21,790
Okay.

319
00:26:35,497 --> 00:26:36,779
The sparks aren’t hot

320
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:40,601
but be careful of the parts
that have already burned.

321
00:26:44,550 --> 00:26:45,550
Here.

322
00:26:52,426 --> 00:26:54,626
Guys, this is a nice background.

323
00:26:54,662 --> 00:26:55,897
Let me take a photo.

324
00:26:57,260 --> 00:26:59,802
- 1…2…
- Mr. Tin!

325
00:27:01,090 --> 00:27:02,712
Wait for us.

326
00:27:02,955 --> 00:27:04,100
Wait for us.

327
00:27:04,128 --> 00:27:06,299
Oh, I’ve been taking
pictures of you two all day.

328
00:27:06,342 --> 00:27:08,263
If you’re tired of us,

329
00:27:08,470 --> 00:27:11,645
take a picture of us
with the president and Ji, then.

330
00:27:11,792 --> 00:27:14,456
Okay, okay. Let’s take a group photo.

331
00:27:14,576 --> 00:27:15,699
- Yeah.
- Hold on.

332
00:27:15,768 --> 00:27:17,143
Tyler, Kongpob!

333
00:27:20,838 --> 00:27:23,626
Ji, I was wondering where you were.
Here you are.

334
00:27:23,739 --> 00:27:25,740
He was hiding from you, you freak.

335
00:27:25,998 --> 00:27:27,478
But you were fooling around with me,
weren’t you?

336
00:27:27,502 --> 00:27:29,656
Cut it out, guys.
Let’s take a picture first.

337
00:27:30,430 --> 00:27:32,001
1…2...

338
00:27:32,028 --> 00:27:34,794
Wait for us, Mr. Tin. Don’t leave us out.

339
00:27:34,828 --> 00:27:35,828
Hey.

340
00:27:36,007 --> 00:27:38,220
This is our class’s photo.
Why are you guys here?

341
00:27:38,522 --> 00:27:40,219
Hey, the president is in my class.

342
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:42,376
- And Kongpob, too.
- Mmm.

343
00:27:42,420 --> 00:27:43,754
They’re from Class 9, right?

344
00:27:43,786 --> 00:27:44,776
Come on.

345
00:27:44,807 --> 00:27:48,099
We haven’t taken a picture together
since middle school.

346
00:27:49,641 --> 00:27:50,920
Hurry, Mr. Tin.

347
00:27:50,952 --> 00:27:52,697
Before too many people want to join in.

348
00:27:52,722 --> 00:27:53,374
Right.

349
00:27:53,617 --> 00:27:54,591
- Come on.
- Hit it.

350
00:27:54,622 --> 00:27:55,696
Ready?

351
00:27:56,106 --> 00:27:57,700
Okay, I’ll start shooting.

352
00:27:57,885 --> 00:28:01,103
When I count to three,
everyone say “Kimchi”, okay?

353
00:28:01,121 --> 00:28:01,776
- Hey?
- What?

354
00:28:01,957 --> 00:28:03,780
We’re at the beach not Korea.

355
00:28:03,881 --> 00:28:04,881
Yeah.

356
00:28:05,469 --> 00:28:06,500
Say “Cheese”, then.

357
00:28:06,730 --> 00:28:09,499
- Yeah, say ‘Cheese’.
- No, I don’t like cheese.

358
00:28:09,540 --> 00:28:10,265
Eh?

359
00:28:10,303 --> 00:28:11,620
But I like it.

360
00:28:11,651 --> 00:28:13,600
Okay, ready? Say “Cheese.”

361
00:28:13,670 --> 00:28:17,601
1…2…3… Cheese!

362
00:28:18,583 --> 00:28:20,202
Atiwitch, look at the camera.

363
00:28:20,727 --> 00:28:23,200
1…2…

364
00:28:23,499 --> 00:28:24,768
Cheese!

365
00:28:38,230 --> 00:28:41,402
(Jiraphat, when you grow up
and have some free time, )

366
00:28:41,597 --> 00:28:43,900
(make sure to go out
with the people close to you.)

367
00:28:47,580 --> 00:28:50,672
(Take lots of pictures
while you still have the chance.)

368
00:28:54,080 --> 00:29:00,490
LESSONS FROM JUNE 30, 2010

369
00:29:19,748 --> 00:29:21,851
(Ask him for a picture.)

370
00:29:24,051 --> 00:29:26,060
(I heard he was drunk driving
and killed someone.)

371
00:29:26,602 --> 00:29:31,103
I checked the yearbook
to find the name of the man who died.

372
00:29:31,139 --> 00:29:33,496
He was a classmate of you two.

373
00:29:33,680 --> 00:29:35,160
The one I couldn’t get in touch with.

374
00:29:42,985 --> 00:29:45,402
Hey, isn’t that Ruth Atiwitch?

375
00:29:51,425 --> 00:29:55,075
(If you’re determined to take this path,
don’t let me see you give up.)

376
00:29:55,115 --> 00:29:59,180
(I’ve seen your work. No matter what,
you’re going to win this award.)

377
00:29:59,355 --> 00:30:02,420
(Don’t listen to that old man.
(I know my son can do it.)

378
00:30:02,530 --> 00:30:05,600
(Ruth, you’re so handsome and kind.)

379
00:30:05,810 --> 00:30:08,099
(Could you spoil
the ending of the drama for us?)

380
00:30:11,748 --> 00:30:15,397
Most of the people who have won this award
are experienced actors.

381
00:30:15,600 --> 00:30:17,001
If you win it,

382
00:30:17,502 --> 00:30:20,179
you’ll be even more successful
than your mother.

383
00:30:23,108 --> 00:30:24,299
What if I don’t want it?

384
00:30:36,425 --> 00:30:39,299
Why don’t you take a break from it
for a while?

385
00:30:47,480 --> 00:30:49,930
We’re going to hang out after this event.
NAWINA HOMECOMING

386
00:30:49,940 --> 00:30:51,097
Wanna join us?

387
00:30:51,620 --> 00:30:53,897
No. I have somewhere I need to be.

388
00:30:54,552 --> 00:30:55,623
Where?

389
00:30:56,420 --> 00:30:57,420
A funeral.

390
00:30:58,939 --> 00:31:00,097
Someone close to you?

391
00:31:00,277 --> 00:31:02,419
Why haven’t I heard anything about it?

392
00:31:03,160 --> 00:31:04,848
It’s an old friend who meant a lot to me.

393
00:31:05,930 --> 00:31:06,951
Old friend?

394
00:31:08,008 --> 00:31:09,902
You have friends other than me?

395
00:31:11,413 --> 00:31:13,398
How long have you known this friend?

396
00:31:31,920 --> 00:31:34,023
You should have seen Mr. Wira’s face

397
00:31:34,730 --> 00:31:37,023
when the president withdrew
from the science project.

398
00:31:37,059 --> 00:31:37,990
He must have been shocked.

399
00:31:38,026 --> 00:31:40,601
Of course. Ruth is the teacher’s protégé.

400
00:31:41,093 --> 00:31:42,896
But the teacher went too far.

401
00:31:43,051 --> 00:31:45,801
He was making the president
work way too hard.

402
00:31:46,480 --> 00:31:48,000
It’s a good thing he withdrew.

403
00:31:48,031 --> 00:31:49,896
Now he’ll have time
to prepare for his exams.

404
00:31:53,309 --> 00:31:55,374
Mmm, this is good.

405
00:31:55,405 --> 00:31:56,445
I want some fried chicken.

406
00:31:56,870 --> 00:31:59,297
- So spicy.
- Yeah, I know, right?

407
00:31:59,410 --> 00:32:01,260
I’ll pass. It doesn’t look good.

408
00:32:01,850 --> 00:32:03,456
I wasn’t gonna share. Just asking.

409
00:32:07,760 --> 00:32:09,850
GRADE 11, CLASS 7

410
00:32:11,011 --> 00:32:16,099
Ked, who’s teaching math today?

411
00:32:16,589 --> 00:32:17,589
Ms. Mai.

412
00:32:17,774 --> 00:32:20,299
Ms. Mai. But who’s Ms. Mai?

413
00:32:20,942 --> 00:32:21,942
She’s Ms. Mai.

414
00:32:22,248 --> 00:32:24,660
I heard you. But who’s the new teacher?

415
00:32:24,764 --> 00:32:25,764
Gun,

416
00:32:25,986 --> 00:32:27,377
I said, Ms. Mai.

417
00:32:27,488 --> 00:32:30,266
I know it’s the new teacher,
not the old one.

418
00:32:30,312 --> 00:32:32,662
I’m not messing with you. It’s Ms. Mai.

419
00:32:32,693 --> 00:32:34,033
- You’re always messing with me.
- Oh.

420
00:32:34,057 --> 00:32:35,299
I mean this new teacher.

421
00:32:37,248 --> 00:32:38,410
The teacher’s here.

422
00:32:41,040 --> 00:32:43,210
MONDAY, JULY 5, 2010

423
00:32:44,709 --> 00:32:45,709
Umm…

424
00:32:47,062 --> 00:32:49,980
Mr. Tin told me you guys were talkative.

425
00:32:50,013 --> 00:32:51,697
Why are you so quiet now?

426
00:32:52,480 --> 00:32:54,697
Attention, students.

427
00:32:55,909 --> 00:32:57,805
Good morning.

428
00:32:58,629 --> 00:32:59,805
Good morning, students.

429
00:33:00,222 --> 00:33:06,019
Starting today, I’ll be teaching math
to the Arts-Languages class.

430
00:33:06,260 --> 00:33:08,131
Oh, I forgot to introduce myself.

431
00:33:08,161 --> 00:33:09,745
I’m Ms. Mai.

432
00:33:10,774 --> 00:33:13,952
I’ll hand out the worksheets now.

433
00:33:14,894 --> 00:33:17,197
Here, please pass them around.

434
00:33:27,151 --> 00:33:28,400
So the answer is…

435
00:33:29,130 --> 00:33:30,195
Can you tell me?

436
00:33:31,070 --> 00:33:33,530
Well done. 720.

437
00:33:34,210 --> 00:33:36,974
I’ll write down the answer for you.

438
00:33:37,905 --> 00:33:38,822
Who got it right?

439
00:33:38,853 --> 00:33:40,145
120 degrees.

440
00:33:40,380 --> 00:33:41,499
Good job.

441
00:33:48,158 --> 00:33:50,382
That’s it for today.

442
00:33:50,545 --> 00:33:51,900
See you next period.

443
00:33:52,180 --> 00:33:55,398
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

444
00:33:57,352 --> 00:33:58,099
Ji.

445
00:33:58,271 --> 00:34:00,457
You asked Ji for help again?

446
00:34:00,755 --> 00:34:03,222
Will you be able to do it on your own
during the actual exam?

447
00:34:04,222 --> 00:34:08,217
If you keep fooling around,
you’ll be in trouble during the exam.

448
00:34:08,962 --> 00:34:11,259
Oh, Ji. Not you too.

449
00:34:11,413 --> 00:34:14,419
There’s plenty of time to study.

450
00:34:15,995 --> 00:34:17,880
Oh, Ji.

451
00:34:18,675 --> 00:34:19,979
What’s wrong with you?

452
00:34:20,198 --> 00:34:22,582
I’ve read the last question three times,

453
00:34:22,607 --> 00:34:24,820
and I still don’t understand
what the poem is about.

454
00:34:24,859 --> 00:34:26,380
I’m going to fail.

455
00:34:26,469 --> 00:34:27,742
- No, you won’t.
- Ahem. Ahem.

456
00:34:29,130 --> 00:34:30,299
Ty, here, buddy.

457
00:34:30,754 --> 00:34:31,754
You want one?

458
00:34:31,850 --> 00:34:32,850
What is it?

459
00:34:32,986 --> 00:34:34,016
My lucky pencil.

460
00:34:34,200 --> 00:34:36,503
It was blessed
for seven days and seven nights.

461
00:34:38,708 --> 00:34:40,715
When choosing an answer, just spin it.

462
00:34:40,758 --> 00:34:42,478
Whichever number shows up,
mark that answer.

463
00:34:42,520 --> 00:34:44,820
Guaranteed to help you pass!
Only 10 baht each.

464
00:34:45,364 --> 00:34:47,598
- Just 10 baht? I’ll take one.
- Only 10 baht.

465
00:34:47,940 --> 00:34:49,819
Next is Mr. Tin’s social studies exam.

466
00:34:50,350 --> 00:34:51,430
It’s all written questions.

467
00:34:51,877 --> 00:34:53,297
- That pencil won’t help.
- Oh.

468
00:34:55,133 --> 00:34:57,020
- Thiti.
- You should have studied for the exam.

469
00:34:57,114 --> 00:34:58,200
Thiti.

470
00:34:58,620 --> 00:35:00,100
You wanna get slapped, Thiti?

471
00:35:00,533 --> 00:35:01,536
Hey, easy.

472
00:35:01,570 --> 00:35:04,496
Thank you for stopping me
or else he would have been dead.

473
00:35:05,060 --> 00:35:06,060
Let’s study.

474
00:35:07,745 --> 00:35:09,416
- Hey, Pim, I’ll borrow that.
- Hey.

475
00:35:10,220 --> 00:35:12,004
Seems like
you don’t need my pencil anymore.

476
00:35:13,320 --> 00:35:15,300
MONDAY, JULY 12

477
00:35:15,342 --> 00:35:18,297
Ji, who used our classroom? It’s so dirty.

478
00:35:18,437 --> 00:35:20,934
Look, there are pen marks
and eraser shavings everywhere.

479
00:35:21,390 --> 00:35:22,502
There’s so much trash, too.

480
00:35:23,391 --> 00:35:24,602
Aren’t you going home?

481
00:35:24,783 --> 00:35:26,308
It’s not your turn to clean today.

482
00:35:26,345 --> 00:35:27,545
You don’t have to wait for me.

483
00:35:27,841 --> 00:35:29,102
Go home and study.

484
00:35:29,912 --> 00:35:33,137
It’s okay, Ji.
There’s plenty of time tomorrow.

485
00:35:33,611 --> 00:35:34,699
Oh, “plenty of time.”

486
00:35:34,945 --> 00:35:36,604
You said that last time, too.

487
00:35:48,942 --> 00:35:49,942
Oh, Ji.

488
00:35:50,562 --> 00:35:52,205
I want to talk to you about something.

489
00:35:53,510 --> 00:35:54,510
What is it?

490
00:35:54,743 --> 00:35:56,955
Umm, well…

491
00:35:57,000 --> 00:35:58,000
Ji.

492
00:35:59,859 --> 00:36:01,936
Can I talk to you outside for a second?

493
00:36:12,210 --> 00:36:15,002
Here, take this.
I just finished coloring it.

494
00:36:19,367 --> 00:36:20,367
Wow.

495
00:36:20,610 --> 00:36:21,610
Is it beautiful?

496
00:36:22,183 --> 00:36:24,219
It is. Why won’t you keep it?

497
00:36:25,788 --> 00:36:28,000
I was going to put it in my portfolio.

498
00:36:28,528 --> 00:36:32,201
But keeping your drawing might make it
look like I have a crush on you.

499
00:36:33,330 --> 00:36:34,626
Nah, that’s cringe.

500
00:36:35,410 --> 00:36:37,900
Besides, you’re not
the only one in the picture.

501
00:36:41,520 --> 00:36:43,106
See? The president’s here.

502
00:36:46,309 --> 00:36:49,625
Is that all
you wanted to talk to me about?

503
00:36:50,176 --> 00:36:52,802
Oh, no. Well…

504
00:36:53,899 --> 00:36:56,201
There’s something I want to tell you
before anyone else.

505
00:36:57,038 --> 00:36:58,038
Before anyone else?

506
00:36:58,705 --> 00:36:59,705
Mmm.

507
00:37:02,872 --> 00:37:05,580
I’ve decided not to apply
to law school anymore.

508
00:37:06,060 --> 00:37:07,060
Huh?

509
00:37:07,610 --> 00:37:08,610
Don’t be surprised.

510
00:37:08,990 --> 00:37:11,401
I’ve decided to apply
to the Faculty of Fine Arts.

511
00:37:11,515 --> 00:37:13,776
I still don’t know which major to choose,

512
00:37:13,810 --> 00:37:15,902
but I think
I’ll have enough time to prepare.

513
00:37:16,780 --> 00:37:21,579
Yesterday, I just canceled
my law tutoring course, and then…

514
00:37:24,500 --> 00:37:26,306
You know
what the Faculty of Fine Arts is, right?

515
00:37:26,330 --> 00:37:27,897
Of course I do.

516
00:37:28,208 --> 00:37:31,200
But why did you suddenly change your mind?

517
00:37:32,362 --> 00:37:33,362
Because of you.

518
00:37:33,777 --> 00:37:34,777
Me?

519
00:37:34,841 --> 00:37:35,841
Yeah.

520
00:37:36,102 --> 00:37:38,192
You were the one who told me that

521
00:37:38,230 --> 00:37:41,002
if I wanted to draw,
I should just do it instead of waiting.

522
00:37:41,154 --> 00:37:43,820
And you also told me
I was definitely going to succeed.

523
00:37:45,583 --> 00:37:48,334
Everyone says
artists don’t make much money

524
00:37:48,367 --> 00:37:50,334
and encourages me to study law.

525
00:37:50,767 --> 00:37:56,600
But you were the first person to praise me
and support me in pursuing this path.

526
00:37:57,360 --> 00:37:58,899
That’s all I wanted to tell you.

527
00:37:59,549 --> 00:38:02,103
If you’re free,
be my model again sometime.

528
00:38:02,820 --> 00:38:04,197
I’ll get going. Bye-bye.

529
00:38:04,905 --> 00:38:05,942
Get home safely, Ji.

530
00:38:14,290 --> 00:38:16,450
You guys are done talking, Ji?
What’s that?

531
00:38:21,045 --> 00:38:22,045
Wow.

532
00:38:23,617 --> 00:38:24,617
Tyler,

533
00:38:26,060 --> 00:38:27,352
what did you want to tell me?

534
00:38:27,988 --> 00:38:30,417
Oh, it’s nothing important, Ji.

535
00:38:30,660 --> 00:38:33,373
At first, my dad was supposed to transfer
overseas for work,

536
00:38:33,940 --> 00:38:35,220
so I was going to move with him.

537
00:38:36,696 --> 00:38:37,696
At first?

538
00:38:37,885 --> 00:38:39,696
Yeah, that was the plan.

539
00:38:40,583 --> 00:38:42,540
But now I’m not moving anymore.

540
00:38:44,760 --> 00:38:45,760
Why not?

541
00:38:45,893 --> 00:38:48,008
Mmm, because of you.

542
00:38:48,290 --> 00:38:50,356
I’ve had so much fun
spending this semester with you.

543
00:38:50,380 --> 00:38:51,285
Kong, too.

544
00:38:51,321 --> 00:38:53,800
When I insisted on staying,
my dad decided not to move either.

545
00:38:53,834 --> 00:38:54,939
Give me a hug.

546
00:38:58,285 --> 00:38:59,697
Why? You’re not happy?

547
00:38:59,730 --> 00:39:01,197
I’m going to throw this away.

548
00:39:01,340 --> 00:39:02,340
See you later.

549
00:39:09,611 --> 00:39:11,801
(When did everything start going wrong?)

550
00:39:13,134 --> 00:39:16,000
(I’m glad Tyler isn’t moving away.)

551
00:39:17,607 --> 00:39:20,010
(I’m glad Pim gets to do what she loves.)

552
00:39:21,571 --> 00:39:26,020
(But what if their futures
fall apart because of me?)

553
00:39:32,008 --> 00:39:33,008
Oh, no!

554
00:39:36,760 --> 00:39:37,760
Ruth.

555
00:39:42,008 --> 00:39:44,000
Be careful. You’re gonna hurt yourself.

556
00:39:47,750 --> 00:39:48,750
Thank you.

557
00:40:09,037 --> 00:40:10,037
Are you okay?

558
00:40:11,644 --> 00:40:13,497
Yeah, I’m fine.

559
00:40:14,133 --> 00:40:16,499
I just missed a step.

560
00:40:47,208 --> 00:40:49,401
Oh, how’s it going?

561
00:40:50,020 --> 00:40:51,620
Are you getting used to this school yet?

562
00:40:52,157 --> 00:40:54,202
I’m still adjusting.

563
00:40:54,797 --> 00:40:57,601
Have you finished grading the exams?

564
00:40:58,949 --> 00:41:00,001
Far from it.

565
00:41:00,398 --> 00:41:03,699
Their answers are giving me a headache.

566
00:41:04,010 --> 00:41:06,500
Is grading exams really that stressful?

567
00:41:07,120 --> 00:41:08,780
You look so stressed.

568
00:41:09,660 --> 00:41:11,401
It’s not just about the exams.

569
00:41:13,380 --> 00:41:14,380
Sorry?

570
00:41:19,681 --> 00:41:22,848
(I’ve only just realized
how badly my hands are shaking.)

571
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:30,299
(It’s because I’m confused,
and more than that, I’m afraid.)

572
00:41:31,869 --> 00:41:37,145
(Afraid that my very existence is ruining
someone’s life and future.)

573
00:41:38,807 --> 00:41:42,660
(Does someone like me
really deserve a second chance?)

574
00:41:54,840 --> 00:41:57,198
Here, drink this.

575
00:41:58,910 --> 00:41:59,998
It’ll help you calm down.

576
00:42:14,340 --> 00:42:16,874
I don’t know what you’re going through,

577
00:42:19,370 --> 00:42:21,096
but I believe everything will be okay.

578
00:42:26,790 --> 00:42:30,253
You can tell me about it
when you’re ready.

579
00:42:34,293 --> 00:42:35,296
But for now…

580
00:42:52,644 --> 00:42:55,500
Just relax and take a deep breath.

581
00:43:33,430 --> 00:43:34,296
All done.

582
00:43:34,320 --> 00:43:35,320
Wow.

583
00:43:35,850 --> 00:43:36,905
It’s beautiful.

584
00:43:37,750 --> 00:43:38,750
You like it?

585
00:43:40,330 --> 00:43:41,536
I know, Ji.

586
00:43:42,710 --> 00:43:43,710
Know what?

587
00:43:44,081 --> 00:43:45,459
It’s Ruth, right?
